WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
MkvDrama.net

3
00:00.210 --> 00:02.620
I'm Saming, Thear's old friend.

4
00:02.820 --> 00:04.410
You never told me about him.

5
00:04.430 --> 00:05.880
I'd completely forgotten he existed.

6
00:05.900 --> 00:07.030
I only remembered when I saw him.

7
00:07.050 --> 00:08.450
I'd love to take a trip down memory lane.

8
00:08.820 --> 00:10.710
All talk, huh?

9
00:11.050 --> 00:12.810
How about we settle this with our fists, you bastard?

10
00:12.830 --> 00:14.080
You bet.

11
00:14.100 --> 00:15.820
You always take what belongs to someone else.

12
00:15.860 --> 00:17.420
Jeez, enough already!

13
00:18.000 --> 00:19.760
You're both drunk. Just go home already.

14
00:20.140 --> 00:21.820
The Black Bull...

15
00:21.850 --> 00:23.490
won't let themselves be caught easily.

16
00:23.600 --> 00:24.940
The only way to catch them

17
00:25.320 --> 00:27.120
is when they actually want to be caught.

18
00:27.150 --> 00:29.820
I suspect that Saming is a mole working for the Black Bull.

19
00:29.970 --> 00:30.870
(Provincial Police Training Center 5)

20
00:30.900 --> 00:32.140
(5 years ago)

21
00:32.170 --> 00:34.610
Endure! Don't waver!

22
00:34.630 --> 00:35.330
Louder!

23
00:35.350 --> 00:37.930
Endure! Don't waver!

24
00:37.950 --> 00:41.180
- All together now! - Endure! Don't waver!

25
00:41.600 --> 00:44.230
Endure! Don't waver!

26
00:44.410 --> 00:45.880
Squad, halt!

27
00:48.160 --> 00:50.160
Everyone, right turn!

28
00:57.250 --> 00:58.270
Wake up!

29
01:04.470 --> 01:05.490
Stand up straight.

30
01:06.380 --> 01:07.060
Yes, sir.

31
01:17.990 --> 01:18.840
Hey, man.

32
01:19.360 --> 01:20.050
Yeah, you.

33
01:20.660 --> 01:21.930
I'm freaking sleepy.

34
01:22.640 --> 01:24.360
I've never had to wake up this early in my life.

35
01:26.550 --> 01:27.800
You just have to get used to it.

36
01:28.060 --> 01:29.830
We'll be waking up early like this for months.

37
01:32.830 --> 01:33.800
Who just yawned?

38
01:40.550 --> 01:41.680
Did you yawn?

39
01:43.720 --> 01:44.560
Yes, sir.

40
01:45.270 --> 01:46.230
Are you sleepy?

41
01:47.390 --> 01:48.060
Yes, sir.

42
01:48.250 --> 01:49.680
What were you doing last night? Why didn't you sleep?

43
01:50.350 --> 01:51.430
I couldn't sleep, sir.

44
01:53.190 --> 01:55.010
Then I guess I have to wake you up.

45
02:00.430 --> 02:02.530
Hey! Your friend is sleepy.

46
02:02.900 --> 02:04.250
Get into push-up position!

47
02:09.050 --> 02:10.680
It's just a yawn. What are we supposed to do?

48
02:11.070 --> 02:13.420
Hey! Attention!

49
02:20.380 --> 02:21.240
What was that?

50
02:23.900 --> 02:25.680
I'm asking you, what were you saying?

51
02:26.800 --> 02:29.450
I was just saying that yawning is hard to control.

52
02:29.800 --> 02:32.300
We shouldn't be punished for it.

53
02:33.770 --> 02:36.210
It's your own body. Why can't you control it?

54
02:36.800 --> 02:39.830
Sleepiness, yawning, sneezing, you should be able to control them all.

55
02:40.390 --> 02:42.060
If you can't even control your own body,

56
02:42.230 --> 02:43.600
then what the hell are you good for?

57
02:45.450 --> 02:46.470
As police officers,

58
02:46.780 --> 02:48.930
are we forbidden from yawning or feeling sleepy?

59
02:51.000 --> 02:52.000
Are you talking back to me?

60
02:52.940 --> 02:54.070
Are you trying to be a smart-ass?

61
02:54.560 --> 02:55.500
I'm not.

62
02:56.600 --> 02:57.850
Just wanted to say how great you are.

63
02:58.300 --> 03:00.010
You never yawn, never feel tired.

64
03:00.600 --> 03:01.920
You're like a total superhuman.

65
03:02.850 --> 03:04.050
Permission to give you a round of applause?

66
03:08.740 --> 03:09.790
What's your name?

67
03:10.270 --> 03:11.180
It's Mungkorn, sir.

68
03:11.940 --> 03:14.000
Mungkorn Phianwanich.

69
03:14.960 --> 03:17.580
Mr. Mungkorn, are you sleepy right now?

70
03:17.630 --> 03:19.360
Yes, sir. But I can handle it.

71
03:20.440 --> 03:21.870
I'm usually an early riser anyway.

72
03:21.970 --> 03:23.260
No, no, no.

73
03:23.780 --> 03:25.210
Being an early riser doesn't matter.

74
03:26.110 --> 03:28.280
If you're sleepy, you get to sleep.

75
03:28.500 --> 03:31.070
Coming to police training is just like a vacation, right?

76
03:31.210 --> 03:32.660
If you want to rest, you should be allowed to rest.

77
03:33.710 --> 03:35.180
Of course, Mr. Mungkorn.

78
03:35.520 --> 03:37.430
I'll make sure you get all the rest you need.

79
03:47.050 --> 03:47.690
Run!

80
03:47.900 --> 03:49.270
Run! Move it!

81
03:50.050 --> 03:52.800
Endure! Don't waver!

82
03:53.210 --> 03:55.980
Endure! Don't waver!

83
03:57.220 --> 03:58.760
Don't waver!

84
03:59.200 --> 04:01.740
Endure! Don't waver!

85
04:01.870 --> 04:02.820
Mr. Mungkorn.

86
04:03.780 --> 04:05.480
You can sleep in until noon.

87
04:05.800 --> 04:06.820
Make yourself at home.

88
04:07.190 --> 04:09.100
I'll bring breakfast to your bedside.

89
04:13.930 --> 04:15.820
Damn, you're really picking on him now.

90
04:15.950 --> 04:17.020
It was just a yawn.

91
04:17.320 --> 04:18.950
Did you have to make him lie in the sun on the concrete?

92
04:19.580 --> 04:21.190
The kid talked back, for crying out loud.

93
04:21.550 --> 04:23.000
I just told them to do push-ups.

94
04:23.620 --> 04:24.630
To wake them up.

95
04:27.610 --> 04:28.530
I like him.

96
04:29.090 --> 04:30.020
He's got guts.

97
04:31.260 --> 04:33.260
The kid actually dared to challenge your authority.

98
04:36.650 --> 04:37.960
You're into that?

99
04:42.040 --> 04:44.060
Ugh, it's freezing out here.

100
04:44.540 --> 04:46.150
Hey, it's cold. I'm afraid you'll get sick.

101
04:46.180 --> 04:47.110
Huddle up. Give each other a hug.

102
04:49.870 --> 04:51.330
Hug him, too.

103
04:51.600 --> 04:52.400
You love your friend, don't you?

104
05:02.480 --> 05:04.440
Wow, you can actually sleep here?

105
05:20.790 --> 05:23.770
(Yin as Theartha)

106
05:28.700 --> 05:31.430
(War as Mungkorn)

107
05:35.570 --> 05:37.920
(Shane as Phuwin)

108
05:38.350 --> 05:41.390
(Boss as Lukplub)

109
05:43.770 --> 05:45.500
(Kit as Kanin)

110
05:45.760 --> 05:47.710
(Tang as Nadol)

111
05:51.190 --> 05:56.430
(Tae as Saming)

112
06:25.100 --> 06:27.670
I looked up some info on that rookie, Mungkorn.

113
06:28.430 --> 06:29.840
He's a kid from Phayao.

114
06:29.870 --> 06:31.060
His father was a veteran cop.

115
06:31.610 --> 06:33.240
So he wants to follow in his dad's footsteps.

116
06:33.770 --> 06:34.540
Whoa.

117
06:35.550 --> 06:38.380
Do you like him so much that you had to dig up his background?

118
06:38.720 --> 06:40.960
Damn, we're instructors. It's against the rules.

119
06:41.070 --> 06:44.100
Hold on, what do we call that again?

120
06:44.760 --> 06:46.500
"An abuse of power"?

121
06:46.920 --> 06:48.240
I know that.

122
06:48.670 --> 06:50.820
I'm just keeping an eye on him. I haven't done anything yet.

123
06:51.490 --> 06:53.280
I'm impressed by the kid.

124
06:53.470 --> 06:54.790
I want to get to know him better.

125
06:54.890 --> 06:56.810
We'll see where it goes.

126
06:57.950 --> 06:59.050
Whatever floats your boat.

127
06:59.400 --> 07:01.560
Not my type. Not at all.

128
07:01.910 --> 07:03.250
My type is over there.

129
07:03.990 --> 07:05.450
Look at that tigress.

130
07:08.920 --> 07:12.260
You really never stop being a player, do you?

131
07:12.830 --> 07:14.030
I'm asking you seriously.

132
07:14.240 --> 07:16.040
Is anyone ever going to be able to stop you?

133
07:16.590 --> 07:17.650
No one, buddy.

134
07:17.810 --> 07:20.970
A guy like me was born to be a gift to all the beautiful people.

135
07:22.710 --> 07:23.580
Good.

136
07:24.340 --> 07:26.000
Then we won't have to compete.

137
07:30.680 --> 07:31.580
So, anyway,

138
07:32.340 --> 07:35.020
is your dad going to help you get promoted?

139
07:35.140 --> 07:37.860
You're lucky as hell.

140
07:38.200 --> 07:39.410
Having a high-ranking father.

141
07:39.970 --> 07:40.990
Dammit.

142
07:41.370 --> 07:42.770
I don't take shortcuts.

143
07:43.040 --> 07:44.610
I do everything by the book.

144
07:44.700 --> 07:46.320
I don't use any special privileges.

145
07:50.320 --> 07:52.260
Alright, get some sleep.

146
07:52.850 --> 07:54.530
We have training early tomorrow morning.

147
08:06.750 --> 08:08.580
What's wrong, Mungkorn? Can't sleep?

148
08:09.800 --> 08:11.000
I'm just starving.

149
08:11.180 --> 08:12.960
Man, same here.

150
08:13.390 --> 08:14.860
Dinner didn't fill me up at all.

151
08:15.590 --> 08:16.710
Who's talking?

152
08:17.260 --> 08:18.560
I told you to sleep, but you're still awake.

153
08:20.140 --> 08:21.350
You guys want to go for a run instead?

154
08:35.610 --> 08:36.400
Mungkorn.

155
08:36.940 --> 08:37.610
Mungkorn.

156
08:37.670 --> 08:38.300
Yeah?

157
08:38.940 --> 08:40.830
Let's head out. Let's go find something to eat.

158
08:41.180 --> 08:42.510
No way.

159
08:42.700 --> 08:44.550
If we're caught sneaking out,

160
08:44.910 --> 08:46.280
we'll get punished again.

161
08:46.350 --> 08:48.480
We won't. I've done it before.

162
08:49.020 --> 08:49.920
I know a shortcut.

163
08:50.270 --> 08:51.450
Please? Come on.

164
08:59.190 --> 09:00.220
Alright, fine. I'm in.

165
09:00.490 --> 09:01.190
Let's go.

166
09:02.130 --> 09:02.810
Let's move.

167
09:23.160 --> 09:24.450
That's much better.

168
09:25.200 --> 09:27.600
I really didn't get enough to eat at dinner.

169
09:27.630 --> 09:30.010
Totally. That lady's cooking was awful.

170
09:30.030 --> 09:31.260
Just imagine

171
09:32.160 --> 09:34.860
if we had an egg and some Vietnamese sausage...

172
09:34.880 --> 09:38.050
Man, that would be a godsend.

173
09:38.880 --> 09:39.710
Keep dreaming.

174
09:39.730 --> 09:41.040
Yeah, this will have to do for now.

175
09:42.810 --> 09:44.340
But you know how it is, right?

176
09:44.520 --> 09:46.910
Getting promoted in this line of work is hard as hell.

177
09:47.400 --> 09:51.270
If there's any shortcut,

178
09:51.720 --> 09:52.500
I'll take it.

179
09:52.780 --> 09:53.800
Check this out.

180
09:54.270 --> 09:56.400
I went to see a shaman in Chiang Rai.

181
09:57.740 --> 09:58.540
Look.

182
10:00.450 --> 10:02.240
I got this sacred charm.

183
10:02.720 --> 10:03.500
See?

184
10:03.860 --> 10:05.870
No way, are you really into that superstitious stuff?

185
10:06.110 --> 10:08.310
- Hey! - I don't believe in that nonsense.

186
10:08.330 --> 10:10.050
I only believe in myself.

187
10:10.070 --> 10:12.950
I'm the one who controls my destiny. It's my own rhythm.

188
10:13.900 --> 10:14.940
Don't believe me? Watch.

189
10:15.410 --> 10:16.970
Check out my rhythm.

190
10:17.680 --> 10:19.120
Really? Your rhythm.

191
10:20.370 --> 10:23.770
Man, your rhythm is way off.

192
10:23.880 --> 10:26.140
- I'm dancing for that tigress. - You idiot.

193
10:34.490 --> 10:35.460
Hey, Saming.

194
10:35.480 --> 10:36.140
Hmm?

195
10:36.390 --> 10:37.210
Sh*t.

196
10:37.830 --> 10:39.030
Isn't that the rookie you got your eye on?

197
10:41.080 --> 10:41.930
Is it?

198
10:43.550 --> 10:44.960
This is going to be fun.

199
10:46.580 --> 10:47.500
Eating at this hour?

200
10:49.060 --> 10:50.420
Hey, slow down. Don't choke on your food.

201
10:50.440 --> 10:51.670
Easy, guys.

202
10:53.440 --> 10:55.380
You realize you're breaking the rules?

203
10:55.630 --> 10:57.630
Sneaking out of the dorm late at night like this.

204
11:00.050 --> 11:01.320
We were hungry, sir.

205
11:02.010 --> 11:03.020
So we couldn't sleep.

206
11:03.260 --> 11:04.690
I see.

207
11:05.070 --> 11:07.190
Couldn't control your own body, huh?

208
11:07.400 --> 11:08.500
So you had to break the rules.

209
11:09.070 --> 11:09.820
So cool.

210
11:14.550 --> 11:16.820
How should I punish you guys?

211
11:17.540 --> 11:20.070
Do you even have the right to?

212
11:20.550 --> 11:21.340
I sure do.

213
11:22.020 --> 11:23.380
I'm your instructor, after all.

214
11:24.070 --> 11:25.710
Aren't you guys off duty yet?

215
11:26.270 --> 11:27.900
And if you're still on the clock,

216
11:29.160 --> 11:30.700
how can you justify drinking like this?

217
11:36.420 --> 11:38.120
Well, we're off duty now.

218
11:38.320 --> 11:39.600
Oh, if you're off duty,

219
11:41.550 --> 11:43.250
then what right do you have to give us orders?

220
11:45.870 --> 11:48.890
Am I even supposed to follow them?

221
11:50.760 --> 11:53.490
Watch that smart mouth of yours, or you're going to regret it.

222
11:55.140 --> 11:56.990
You reek of booze.

223
11:58.390 --> 11:59.440
Regret what exactly?

224
11:59.890 --> 12:00.800
Go ahead and tell me.

225
12:02.820 --> 12:04.340
Thear, take it easy.

226
12:08.100 --> 12:10.000
If the higher-ups hear about this, we'll all be in deep trouble.

227
12:10.030 --> 12:11.660
That's a lot of empty bottles.

228
12:12.860 --> 12:14.790
You've already had your dinner.

229
12:14.820 --> 12:15.880
Aren't you full yet?

230
12:18.010 --> 12:19.910
I was the one who was still hungry, sir.

231
12:20.160 --> 12:22.150
Mungkorn just came along to keep me company.

232
12:22.630 --> 12:23.980
Please don't punish him.

233
12:24.540 --> 12:26.660
Alright, it's fine.

234
12:27.730 --> 12:29.370
We'll let it slide this time,

235
12:29.900 --> 12:32.080
but don't let it happen again. Alright?

236
12:32.910 --> 12:33.590
Yes, sir.

237
12:33.790 --> 12:34.780
Hey, Saming.

238
12:35.000 --> 12:36.210
Aren't you being a bit too soft on them?

239
12:36.360 --> 12:37.580
They're going to start getting cocky.

240
12:37.600 --> 12:39.260
Man, just chill out.

241
12:39.280 --> 12:40.720
The kids were just hungry.

242
12:40.750 --> 12:42.540
Don't go ruining their futures over this.

243
12:44.950 --> 12:46.630
Alright, you two, head back and get some sleep.

244
12:47.130 --> 12:49.410
Thank you so much for understanding, sir.

245
12:49.740 --> 12:51.010
We won't do it again, I promise.

246
12:51.050 --> 12:51.940
Thank you, sir.

247
12:52.940 --> 12:54.210
Go on, move it.

248
12:55.930 --> 12:56.730
Hey.

249
13:01.650 --> 13:02.780
With an attitude like that,

250
13:03.200 --> 13:04.730
you'd better watch out when you run into the wrong person.

251
13:05.140 --> 13:07.040
Not everyone is going to be as nice as we are.

252
13:08.850 --> 13:11.560
Thanks for the life lesson, sir.

253
13:12.930 --> 13:15.590
But when you get back, make sure to drink plenty of water.

254
13:16.370 --> 13:18.030
It'll help with the hangover.

255
13:23.360 --> 13:24.210
Let's get some sleep.

256
13:24.230 --> 13:25.690
- Come on. - Let's go, man.

257
13:26.190 --> 13:27.040
Let's go.

258
13:27.320 --> 13:28.450
Move it, buddy.

259
13:28.800 --> 13:30.510
I think I'm going to have some really good dreams tonight.

260
13:30.530 --> 13:31.910
Dreaming about who, exactly?

261
13:31.930 --> 13:33.090
You're in for it tomorrow.

262
13:33.110 --> 13:36.180
(Interrogation Station)

263
13:47.490 --> 13:48.370
Good Morning.

264
13:49.980 --> 13:52.670
You are the suspect, Mr. Saming ChanJong, correct?

265
13:53.170 --> 13:53.990
That's right.

266
13:58.180 --> 14:01.930
You've been charged with theft.

267
14:02.030 --> 14:05.220
A report has been filed stating that you stole a wallet.

268
14:05.750 --> 14:08.030
Could you please explain exactly what was taken?

269
14:08.200 --> 14:09.740
No, I didn't steal anything.

270
14:11.600 --> 14:12.830
How can you say that?

271
14:12.850 --> 14:15.980
The report clearly states that you're the one who stole the wallet.

272
14:16.620 --> 14:18.390
And what evidence do you have?

273
14:19.360 --> 14:20.810
I have plenty of money of my own.

274
14:21.040 --> 14:22.560
I have no reason to steal at all.

275
14:25.020 --> 14:25.820
Wait.

276
14:35.620 --> 14:37.120
Don't give up yet.

277
14:37.150 --> 14:38.610
Keep pressing me. Hurry!

278
14:39.270 --> 14:41.020
Press how, exactly?

279
14:41.490 --> 14:43.030
You already said you didn't steal.

280
14:43.130 --> 14:44.610
And there isn't enough evidence.

281
14:45.070 --> 14:46.140
So that's the end of it.

282
14:46.500 --> 14:49.570
Just try some small talk.

283
14:50.150 --> 14:53.630
I might relax and slip up with some important info.

284
14:54.300 --> 14:55.040
Okay?

285
14:55.090 --> 14:56.140
Alright.

286
15:06.450 --> 15:08.940
Did you know the victim before?

287
15:11.370 --> 15:12.800
Are you two dating?

288
15:12.820 --> 15:13.740
No.

289
15:14.670 --> 15:15.900
I'm still single.

290
15:17.260 --> 15:18.900
And do you live alone?

291
15:19.110 --> 15:19.950
Yes.

292
15:20.410 --> 15:21.900
I live alone.

293
15:22.330 --> 15:23.680
And I'm very lonely.

294
15:26.240 --> 15:27.820
You must have plenty of money to spare

295
15:28.240 --> 15:29.720
if you don't have to support anyone.

296
15:31.780 --> 15:34.970
So, do you want me to look after you?

297
15:35.000 --> 15:36.470
Are you a player?

298
15:36.490 --> 15:37.920
Oh, not at all.

299
15:38.560 --> 15:40.200
I'm not like Thear.

300
15:42.050 --> 15:43.900
Hey, Instructor!

301
15:44.590 --> 15:45.500
What do I have to do with this?

302
15:50.570 --> 15:51.630
In that case,

303
15:52.610 --> 15:54.610
can you write something on my arm?

304
15:54.630 --> 15:55.930
Actually, never mind.

305
15:56.500 --> 15:58.100
Write it on this paper for me instead.

306
15:58.810 --> 16:00.050
Write "Already taken."

307
16:03.730 --> 16:05.320
(Already taken.)

308
16:06.830 --> 16:07.650
Thank you.

309
16:16.910 --> 16:18.780
You're definitely the one who stole it.

310
16:18.950 --> 16:20.550
What? I don't understand.

311
16:22.160 --> 16:23.890
Well, the owner of these bills

312
16:23.920 --> 16:25.950
wrote "Already taken" on every single one of them.

313
16:25.980 --> 16:27.150
On every single bill.

314
16:27.170 --> 16:28.980
And I checked the handwriting.

315
16:29.790 --> 16:31.090
It doesn't match at all.

316
16:31.710 --> 16:33.100
Wait, that’s not right.

317
16:33.220 --> 16:34.480
I've checked every single one.

318
16:34.510 --> 16:36.640
I didn't see that handwriting at all.

319
16:39.560 --> 16:41.760
You just confessed that you're the one who took it.

320
16:42.540 --> 16:43.890
So you checked every single one?

321
16:45.550 --> 16:46.350
Dammit.

322
16:47.780 --> 16:49.120
I accidentally confessed after all.

323
16:50.510 --> 16:52.180
Catching me with my guard down?

324
16:54.720 --> 16:55.620
Here.

325
16:56.280 --> 16:57.300
A perfect ten.

326
17:00.420 --> 17:01.630
Thank you, Saming.

327
17:02.770 --> 17:03.920
Everything you've taught me,

328
17:04.060 --> 17:05.950
I'll put it to the best use possible.

329
17:06.400 --> 17:08.370
Did you just go easy on the kid?

330
17:08.400 --> 17:10.540
Weren't you a bit too easy to trick, Instructor Saming?

331
17:10.560 --> 17:11.900
What do you mean?

332
17:12.020 --> 17:13.410
The kid is actually talented.

333
17:13.640 --> 17:15.440
I just gave him a little nudge.

334
17:16.270 --> 17:17.660
You're that good, huh?

335
17:17.900 --> 17:19.500
Care to teach me sometime?

336
17:19.950 --> 17:21.330
I'm the mean one.

337
17:21.830 --> 17:23.100
So no one really listens to me.

338
17:31.260 --> 17:32.030
You did great.

339
17:32.060 --> 17:32.940
I almost failed.

340
17:34.030 --> 17:35.000
You're doing fine.

341
17:35.500 --> 17:36.820
- Really? - Yeah.

342
17:42.000 --> 17:43.380
Mungkorn.

343
17:44.230 --> 17:47.530
Actually, Instructor Thear isn't such a bad trainer.

344
17:47.750 --> 17:50.230
But you're being such a smart-ass to him.

345
17:52.320 --> 17:54.440
But I think he's too full of himself.

346
17:54.570 --> 17:55.370
Hey.

347
17:55.890 --> 18:00.030
But I've heard rumors that girls are all over him.

348
18:00.730 --> 18:03.720
I mean, just look at him. He's got the looks and the money.

349
18:03.740 --> 18:05.820
Man, even I'm getting flustered.

350
18:06.390 --> 18:08.400
He could have anyone he wanted.

351
18:09.720 --> 18:12.330
No wonder he's so confident then.

352
18:13.970 --> 18:17.100
But he's really not my cup of tea.

353
18:18.690 --> 18:21.070
I prefer someone who's more humble.

354
18:38.800 --> 18:40.140
Wait, Tri?

355
18:40.800 --> 18:41.950
Where's my towel?

356
18:44.180 --> 18:45.800
Hey, are you pulling a prank on me?

357
18:46.120 --> 18:47.420
Hey, Tri!

358
18:48.590 --> 18:49.730
Is anyone there?

359
18:50.280 --> 18:51.960
Hey, anybody! Is anyone there?

360
19:43.070 --> 19:44.340
What is up with you?

361
19:45.220 --> 19:47.280
Are you some kind of creep? Are you looking for an audience?

362
19:47.620 --> 19:49.020
I'm not trying to show off.

363
19:49.590 --> 19:50.630
My friends are messing with me.

364
19:51.510 --> 19:54.510
How is that tiny rag supposed to cover you up?

365
19:54.530 --> 19:56.170
Here, take my towel.

366
19:57.220 --> 19:57.820
Go on.

367
19:59.900 --> 20:02.460
If I let go, I'll be butt naked for sure.

368
20:07.090 --> 20:08.630
Can you help me?

369
20:11.730 --> 20:13.120
Fine, have it your way.

370
20:32.970 --> 20:33.760
Thank you.

371
20:36.670 --> 20:38.410
I finally got a glimpse of "Little Mungkorn."

372
20:38.430 --> 20:40.270
Hey, it's not "little," you know.

373
20:40.330 --> 20:41.700
I was just teasing.

374
20:49.260 --> 20:50.770
And why are you using this bathroom?

375
20:50.850 --> 20:52.180
There's an instructors' bathroom.

376
20:53.230 --> 20:55.030
The water in that one isn't running.

377
20:55.430 --> 20:57.490
So I came here to shower in peace.

378
20:58.890 --> 21:00.900
Funnily enough, I stumbled upon a real treat.

379
21:05.940 --> 21:08.530
If your friends prank you, you should get back at them.

380
21:10.120 --> 21:11.740
But then again, someone like you

381
21:12.480 --> 21:14.500
doesn't seem like the type to hold a grudge.

382
21:15.210 --> 21:18.150
From what I can tell, anyone who gets close to you is bound to like you.

383
21:22.080 --> 21:23.380
That's just how I am.

384
21:24.080 --> 21:25.240
I like helping people,

385
21:26.320 --> 21:27.990
even if it could get me into trouble.

386
21:29.640 --> 21:30.970
Just look at my friend.

387
21:31.380 --> 21:32.740
He betrayed me just like that.

388
21:37.040 --> 21:38.710
I'll give the towel back right away.

389
21:40.640 --> 21:42.140
Go ahead. I'll wait right here.

390
21:56.280 --> 21:58.670
(Shooting Station)

391
22:22.050 --> 22:24.140
Hey, you've been aiming for ages. Why haven't you fired?

392
22:26.340 --> 22:27.960
I was just adjusting my stance.

393
22:29.370 --> 22:30.450
Here, let me show you.

394
22:31.780 --> 22:32.520
Look.

395
22:33.210 --> 22:34.490
Step your left foot out a bit.

396
22:36.140 --> 22:37.490
Keep your shoulders relaxed.

397
22:41.410 --> 22:43.860
Why do you look even more tense now?

398
22:44.230 --> 22:45.430
I'm just not used to this, sir.

399
22:45.740 --> 22:46.930
You're too close.

400
22:50.190 --> 22:51.550
When you're holding a gun,

401
22:52.230 --> 22:53.320
don't grip it with your whole hand.

402
22:53.760 --> 22:55.600
When pulling the trigger, use only your finger.

403
22:57.260 --> 22:58.100
So the gun stays in place.

404
23:00.290 --> 23:01.040
Whoa!

405
23:02.520 --> 23:04.270
Uh, Instructor Saming, sir.

406
23:04.980 --> 23:06.190
My gun is jammed.

407
23:06.220 --> 23:07.680
Could you please take a look?

408
23:07.710 --> 23:08.680
Yeah, I'm coming.

409
23:10.190 --> 23:11.540
Don't fire yet. Wait for me.

410
23:18.140 --> 23:19.600
Reload and keep firing.

411
23:25.700 --> 23:26.780
With a grip like that,

412
23:27.180 --> 23:28.740
you could shoot all day and never hit anything.

413
23:32.150 --> 23:33.850
I'll just wait for Instructor Saming to show me, then.

414
23:34.740 --> 23:35.940
It's not like I want to teach you,

415
23:36.400 --> 23:37.880
but watching you is just frustrating.

416
23:39.870 --> 23:41.370
Here, grip it tightly.

417
23:42.980 --> 23:43.870
Squeeze it.

418
23:44.580 --> 23:45.250
Okay.

419
23:47.120 --> 23:47.960
Aim carefully.

420
23:51.500 --> 23:53.050
Look at the target. Why are you looking at me?

421
23:53.760 --> 23:54.830
Squeeze it tight like this.

422
23:55.120 --> 23:56.060
Relax here a bit.

423
23:56.080 --> 23:57.760
Okay, don't tense up your shoulders.

424
23:58.660 --> 23:59.440
Like this.

425
24:01.320 --> 24:02.920
In your stance, put your left foot forward.

426
24:03.900 --> 24:04.730
Put your right foot back.

427
24:06.780 --> 24:08.040
There, squeeze it tight.

428
24:10.060 --> 24:11.580
Left side, lean forward.

429
24:12.300 --> 24:13.060
Yeah.

430
24:16.620 --> 24:17.350
Lean into it.

431
24:18.580 --> 24:20.040
The gun itself isn't dangerous.

432
24:20.220 --> 24:21.340
It doesn't just go off by itself.

433
24:22.020 --> 24:23.820
It's the person who lacks confidence that's dangerous.

434
24:24.930 --> 24:27.970
Once the front and rear sights are aligned, slowly pull.

435
24:28.890 --> 24:30.090
Slowly draw it back.

436
24:30.110 --> 24:31.490
Keep exhaling slowly.

437
24:35.150 --> 24:36.020
Slowly draw.

438
24:37.920 --> 24:38.750
Easy.

439
24:39.970 --> 24:40.910
Exhale.

440
24:48.650 --> 24:49.330
Wow.

441
24:50.020 --> 24:51.240
Not a bullseye, but pretty close.

442
24:51.270 --> 24:52.440
You have a good instructor.

443
25:02.000 --> 25:03.500
Oh? You can shoot now?

444
25:05.590 --> 25:07.420
Instructor Thear came over to teach me, sir.

445
25:09.810 --> 25:10.810
It's not like I wanted to teach him.

446
25:10.830 --> 25:12.230
Watching him was just getting on my nerves.

447
25:12.250 --> 25:13.430
His technique was a total disaster.

448
25:33.070 --> 25:34.540
Next time you need something, let me know first.

449
25:35.610 --> 25:36.550
Thank you, sir.

450
25:40.160 --> 25:45.470
(3 months later)

451
25:45.490 --> 25:48.270
Hey, man, I got a really good amulet.

452
25:48.700 --> 25:50.620
Someone recommended it to me from a temple in Chiang Mai.

453
25:50.930 --> 25:54.390
They say it protects you and keeps all the bad luck away.

454
25:54.970 --> 25:57.120
And I even asked for a soulmate, too.

455
25:57.320 --> 26:00.460
I asked for someone with chubby cheeks and a real cute face.

456
26:01.840 --> 26:03.240
I seriously can't believe it.

457
26:03.820 --> 26:05.510
I can't believe you've actually become this superstitious.

458
26:05.880 --> 26:06.730
Count me out.

459
26:07.980 --> 26:10.140
My life isn't exactly unlucky.

460
26:10.240 --> 26:13.760
As for a soulmate, I can find one myself.

461
26:13.890 --> 26:14.980
Just look at me.

462
26:15.760 --> 26:17.890
Hey, making merit and praying once in a while

463
26:17.920 --> 26:19.530
isn't going to hurt anyone.

464
26:19.810 --> 26:21.710
Your birthday is coming up in two days.

465
26:21.850 --> 26:23.900
Want me to take you to see a respected monk?

466
26:23.930 --> 26:26.090
Get a charm-enhancing ritual? You down?

467
26:26.250 --> 26:27.670
No way, man.

468
26:28.100 --> 26:30.550
My life is mine to determine.

469
26:30.570 --> 26:32.600
No being or god can decide my fate.

470
26:51.360 --> 26:52.700
Hey, time to sleep.

471
26:53.120 --> 26:54.420
Hard training tomorrow.

472
27:36.660 --> 27:37.700
Where did your friend go?

473
27:39.000 --> 27:40.530
I don't know, sir.

474
27:41.050 --> 27:41.910
Probably to the restroom.

475
27:42.280 --> 27:43.460
The restroom?

476
27:44.190 --> 27:45.840
Then why did he set up these blankets to fake being in bed?

477
27:47.530 --> 27:48.900
He snuck out, didn't he?

478
28:43.190 --> 28:43.990
Where have you been?

479
28:45.440 --> 28:46.710
I went to the restroom, sir.

480
28:48.000 --> 28:49.080
The restroom?

481
28:49.890 --> 28:53.180
I had no idea they started selling snacks in the damn restroom stalls.

482
28:53.990 --> 28:55.060
Well, I...

483
28:55.090 --> 28:55.910
Well, what?

484
28:56.200 --> 28:58.660
I told you not to go outside, didn't I?

485
28:59.060 --> 29:00.310
Every place has rules.

486
29:00.520 --> 29:02.240
I'm responsible for your lives.

487
29:02.540 --> 29:03.600
If something happened to you,

488
29:03.620 --> 29:05.700
have you even thought about what I'd have to do?

489
29:06.940 --> 29:08.250
Nothing's going to happen, sir.

490
29:08.830 --> 29:10.260
I can take care of myself.

491
29:10.280 --> 29:12.540
Brilliant. You think you're just the smartest, don't you?

492
29:12.560 --> 29:13.780
You've got a comeback for everything.

493
29:13.800 --> 29:15.180
But don't you dare be a smart-ass with me.

494
29:15.490 --> 29:16.750
Rules are rules.

495
29:16.900 --> 29:19.410
If you don't want to follow them, then don't bother being a cop.

496
29:19.440 --> 29:20.520
Just go home.

497
29:21.880 --> 29:23.530
I was sent here to train you.

498
29:24.400 --> 29:25.850
If you refuse to follow orders,

499
29:26.030 --> 29:27.270
then I've failed in my duty.

500
29:27.850 --> 29:28.970
Don't blame yourself, sir.

501
29:29.480 --> 29:30.500
It's my fault.

502
29:31.130 --> 29:32.560
You have no right to talk back to me.

503
29:33.310 --> 29:36.230
From now on, you will follow my every command.

504
29:36.950 --> 29:39.470
Run fifty laps around the field! Now!

505
29:40.620 --> 29:41.420
Yes, sir!

506
29:42.620 --> 29:43.840
As for the rest of you, go back to sleep.

507
29:52.590 --> 29:54.180
Act wisely!

508
29:54.650 --> 29:56.780
Always stay vigilant!

509
29:56.830 --> 29:57.840
Louder!

510
29:57.890 --> 29:59.320
I made a mistake, sir!

511
30:00.750 --> 30:02.230
I can't hear you! Louder!

512
30:03.690 --> 30:05.290
Act wisely!

513
30:06.110 --> 30:08.100
Always stay vigilant!

514
30:08.120 --> 30:10.710
- I can't hear you! Louder! - I made a mistake, sir!

515
30:14.160 --> 30:15.730
- Speak up! - Act wisely!

516
30:15.770 --> 30:16.710
What happened?

517
30:18.980 --> 30:21.150
The kid snuck out for food again.

518
30:21.170 --> 30:22.670
And what did he promise us both?

519
30:22.700 --> 30:24.100
That he wouldn't do it again.

520
30:24.750 --> 30:27.000
I lost my temper and ordered fifty laps of running.

521
30:27.510 --> 30:29.080
Act wisely!

522
30:30.050 --> 30:32.160
Always stay vigilant!

523
30:32.560 --> 30:34.550
- Act wisely! - Louder!

524
30:34.770 --> 30:36.890
Always stay vigilant!

525
30:37.060 --> 30:39.540
Maybe fifty push-ups would've been enough.

526
30:40.650 --> 30:41.640
It wouldn't be.

527
30:41.750 --> 30:43.190
Do you really think he'd learn his lesson?

528
30:43.410 --> 30:45.110
Act wisely!

529
30:46.640 --> 30:48.780
Always stay vigilant!

530
30:48.810 --> 30:50.000
I made a mistake, sir.

531
30:51.500 --> 30:52.680
Watch your volume!

532
30:52.890 --> 30:54.550
Act wisely!

533
30:55.380 --> 30:57.240
Always stay vigilant!

534
30:57.260 --> 30:57.900
Mungkorn!

535
30:58.160 --> 30:58.900
Hey.

536
31:00.670 --> 31:01.940
If you go in there to help him,

537
31:01.970 --> 31:03.110
what kind of authority will I have left?

538
31:03.480 --> 31:06.230
Do you want him to grow up to be a cop who keeps making the same mistakes?

539
31:07.740 --> 31:08.950
I made a mistake, sir.

540
31:10.460 --> 31:12.050
Act wisely!

541
31:12.620 --> 31:14.790
Always stay vigilant!

542
31:15.670 --> 31:16.820
I think that's enough, man.

543
31:18.880 --> 31:20.640
It looks like the kid can't take it anymore.

544
31:21.840 --> 31:23.310
He's learned his lesson by now.

545
31:23.980 --> 31:25.790
If something happens to him, it'll turn into a huge mess.

546
31:30.300 --> 31:31.730
Fine, it's up to you guys then.

547
31:32.430 --> 31:33.130
Hey!

548
31:37.560 --> 31:39.180
- Act wisely! - That's enough.

549
31:39.420 --> 31:40.270
- Stop. - Mungkorn.

550
31:40.560 --> 31:42.170
That's enough. You can stop now.

551
31:42.460 --> 31:43.580
Go on, go to sleep.

552
31:43.810 --> 31:46.410
No, sir. I have to finish them.

553
31:46.910 --> 31:49.680
Otherwise, people will think I'm getting special treatment.

554
31:50.630 --> 31:52.170
It won't look good for all of you, sir.

555
31:52.740 --> 31:54.370
We know you've learned your lesson.

556
31:55.520 --> 31:56.320
No, sir.

557
31:57.060 --> 31:59.470
Since I've started, I have to get through to the end.

558
32:01.790 --> 32:02.520
Mungkorn.

559
32:04.210 --> 32:05.790
Act wisely!

560
32:06.870 --> 32:09.470
Always stay vigilant!

561
32:10.800 --> 32:12.420
Act wisely!

562
32:13.340 --> 32:15.990
Always stay vigilant!

563
32:18.760 --> 32:20.260
Stand at ease!

564
32:21.640 --> 32:22.850
Don't look so lifeless.

565
32:22.870 --> 32:24.640
We have a lot more training to do.

566
32:25.510 --> 32:26.460
Stay sharp.

567
32:26.850 --> 32:27.790
Awake yet?

568
32:28.440 --> 32:29.680
- Yes, sir! - We're awake, sir!

569
32:34.760 --> 32:36.010
And where is your friend?

570
32:36.260 --> 32:37.300
Why isn't he up for the morning run?

571
32:38.530 --> 32:40.770
Mungkorn is sick, sir. He can't get out of bed.

572
32:45.430 --> 32:47.610
Hey, Saming, lead them for the run.

573
32:47.640 --> 32:48.800
I'll go check on him myself.

574
32:52.090 --> 32:53.050
Squad, attention!

575
32:53.870 --> 32:54.910
Right turn!

576
33:14.190 --> 33:15.080
Mr. Mungkorn.

577
33:24.270 --> 33:25.270
I'm sorry, sir.

578
33:25.750 --> 33:27.000
I overslept.

579
33:28.240 --> 33:30.160
I'll go join the line right away, sir.

580
33:32.340 --> 33:33.290
Wait, hold on.

581
33:34.780 --> 33:35.790
Can you even handle it?

582
33:36.070 --> 33:37.710
Your friend said you were sick.

583
33:38.140 --> 33:38.920
I'm fine, sir.

584
33:39.300 --> 33:40.570
I'm feeling much better now.

585
33:42.320 --> 33:43.660
Don't talk back.

586
33:43.680 --> 33:46.410
I just touched you, and I can tell you've got a fever.

587
33:46.720 --> 33:48.470
If I let you go run in the sun,

588
33:48.960 --> 33:50.240
you'll definitely pass out and die.

589
33:55.030 --> 33:56.110
Just stay in bed and rest.

590
33:56.860 --> 33:59.910
I'll go get some medicine and a cloth to wipe you down.

591
34:00.400 --> 34:01.420
That's not necessary, sir.

592
34:02.700 --> 34:04.200
I'd rather go to the infirmary myself.

593
34:05.870 --> 34:07.390
You really are stubborn, aren't you?

594
34:08.160 --> 34:10.180
Just lie back and rest. I'll take care of it.

595
34:38.620 --> 34:39.650
You really don't have to, sir.

596
34:40.240 --> 34:41.370
I'd rather do it myself.

597
34:42.790 --> 34:44.090
Just stay still, will you?

598
34:45.640 --> 34:47.050
I told you already

599
34:47.220 --> 34:49.120
that I'm responsible for your lives.

600
34:50.370 --> 34:51.840
It was my own fault, anyway.

601
34:53.480 --> 34:54.490
I'm sorry, sir.

602
34:59.600 --> 35:01.020
I hope you understand

603
35:01.040 --> 35:02.150
why I had to punish you.

604
35:03.360 --> 35:06.730
I was sent here to train you all to become police officers.

605
35:08.680 --> 35:10.740
So it's a huge responsibility for me

606
35:11.120 --> 35:13.030
to make your dreams come true.

607
35:15.030 --> 35:16.410
That's why I was so disappointed

608
35:16.810 --> 35:18.580
that I couldn't get you to listen to me.

609
35:19.690 --> 35:21.310
I understand everything now, sir.

610
35:22.980 --> 35:24.610
And I won't let it happen again.

611
35:26.650 --> 35:30.300
But at the very least, I wish you'd be nice to me sometimes.

612
35:33.570 --> 35:37.220
Well, someone has to play the tough and annoying part, right?

613
35:38.010 --> 35:41.210
Let Saming and Phuwin be the nice cops.

614
35:48.430 --> 35:50.440
Go ahead and eat that cake first.

615
35:50.820 --> 35:52.320
You need to have something in your stomach before taking medicine.

616
35:54.460 --> 35:55.570
That's enough, sir.

617
35:57.820 --> 35:59.030
This cake?

618
36:01.370 --> 36:03.750
Actually, it's not for me.

619
36:05.500 --> 36:07.220
Yesterday was your birthday, right?

620
36:09.640 --> 36:11.420
And yet you still had to come out and train us.

621
36:12.040 --> 36:15.090
I just wanted to do something small to show my appreciation.

622
36:16.660 --> 36:18.420
That's why I snuck out to buy this for you.

623
36:19.640 --> 36:22.680
But the shop only had banana cake

624
36:23.200 --> 36:24.740
and these prayer candles.

625
36:31.030 --> 36:32.150
Are you serious?

626
36:32.820 --> 36:34.350
Now, you're really making me feel guilty,

627
36:34.370 --> 36:35.630
especially after I punished you.

628
36:37.740 --> 36:38.780
Not at all.

629
36:39.600 --> 36:41.590
You did everything right.

630
36:42.570 --> 36:43.630
By acting like that,

631
36:44.430 --> 36:46.020
I respect you even more now.

632
36:56.460 --> 36:57.130
Hey.

633
36:58.240 --> 37:00.430
Tri has been sneaking cigarettes.

634
37:01.140 --> 37:02.190
You should put him through some extra drills.

635
37:03.540 --> 37:05.070
See? That’s more like it.

636
37:05.110 --> 37:06.330
He needs to get a taste of his own medicine.

637
37:18.330 --> 37:20.040
Happy Birthday, Instructor Thear.

638
37:24.070 --> 37:25.470
Thank you, Mr. Mungkorn.

639
37:27.980 --> 37:28.950
Wait!

640
37:30.490 --> 37:32.060
Make a wish first.

641
37:33.370 --> 37:34.150
Oh, right.

642
37:34.680 --> 37:35.710
Alright, here goes.

643
37:36.340 --> 37:37.670
I’m not asking for much.

644
37:37.930 --> 37:41.100
I wish for a successful career just like this.

645
37:41.560 --> 37:43.030
To find a great love.

646
37:43.270 --> 37:45.140
A cute, petite partner.

647
37:46.530 --> 37:47.580
And big boobs would be even better.

648
37:49.350 --> 37:51.050
Wow, you certainly have a clear type.

649
37:52.470 --> 37:54.560
Amen to that. May my wish come true.

650
37:55.650 --> 37:58.390
I think we should split it.

651
37:59.660 --> 38:01.700
No way. I bought it for you. You should be the one to eat it.

652
38:01.730 --> 38:03.810
Come on, don't be stubborn. Let's eat together.

653
38:05.510 --> 38:06.370
You have to take your medicine soon.

654
38:06.400 --> 38:08.380
So have some first, so it doesn't upset your stomach.

655
38:11.980 --> 38:13.100
The rest is all yours.

656
38:13.860 --> 38:14.730
Thank you.

657
38:26.240 --> 38:27.930
I should've bought two.

658
38:31.030 --> 38:32.130
Oh, wait.

659
38:33.220 --> 38:35.320
I have one more thing for you.

660
38:36.010 --> 38:36.940
What is it now?

661
38:37.410 --> 38:38.150
Here.

662
38:40.850 --> 38:43.020
I was walking through the market the other day.

663
38:44.840 --> 38:46.450
And I came across this coffee mug.

664
38:47.260 --> 38:50.380
It has the same pattern as yours, just a different color.

665
38:50.410 --> 38:52.860
Here, you can alternate between them.

666
38:53.640 --> 38:54.550
Whoa.

667
38:56.810 --> 38:58.460
You really did all this for me?

668
38:59.240 --> 39:00.160
Thank you.

669
39:00.700 --> 39:01.820
Do you have a thing for me?

670
39:02.530 --> 39:03.970
Hey, I'm into people with big boobies, you know.

671
39:06.140 --> 39:08.080
I don't. I just respect you.

672
39:08.910 --> 39:09.910
Why would I like you?

673
39:11.590 --> 39:12.460
Thank you.

674
39:45.920 --> 39:47.100
(Tower Jump Station)

675
40:04.740 --> 40:06.170
Do you remember what I taught you?

676
40:06.560 --> 40:07.710
I do, sir.

677
40:09.260 --> 40:10.340
Want a little nudge?

678
40:10.360 --> 40:11.410
No, sir.

679
40:14.020 --> 40:15.700
- Can Mungkorn go first? - Hey!

680
40:17.650 --> 40:18.410
Off you go.

681
40:21.690 --> 40:25.270
Here comes Mighty Tri!

682
40:33.850 --> 40:35.160
You got this, Mungkorn.

683
40:35.700 --> 40:37.870
The harness is 100% safe, so don't worry.

684
40:38.070 --> 40:38.690
Okay?

685
40:38.840 --> 40:39.960
I'll be right here watching you.

686
40:41.370 --> 40:44.040
If you're nervous, just take deep breaths in and out.

687
40:44.300 --> 40:45.210
Keep your focus.

688
40:46.100 --> 40:46.940
Got it?

689
40:48.230 --> 40:50.330
My focus is out the window.

690
40:50.880 --> 40:53.080
Once you've jumped, I'll take you out for a meal.

691
40:53.110 --> 40:56.310
Tell me whatever you want to eat, and it's my treat. Okay?

692
40:56.580 --> 40:57.910
I don't want to eat anything.

693
40:58.380 --> 41:00.970
Right now, I'm so nervous I could puke.

694
41:03.110 --> 41:04.010
Want me to push you?

695
41:04.780 --> 41:05.900
No way.

696
41:06.260 --> 41:08.500
If you push me, I'm going to drag you down with me.

697
41:10.530 --> 41:11.330
What's taking so long?

698
41:11.350 --> 41:12.580
(Is something wrong?)

699
41:14.540 --> 41:15.890
Yeah, just chill out.

700
41:15.920 --> 41:17.780
Let him get it together first.

701
41:19.030 --> 41:21.240
Ugh, if you're that scared, just go home.

702
41:21.850 --> 41:23.030
(Go do something else.)

703
41:23.050 --> 41:24.700
(Why bother being a cop if you're just going to get in the way?)

704
41:24.730 --> 41:25.860
You're wasting everyone else's time.

705
41:34.800 --> 41:36.310
Why do you have to yell at me?

706
41:36.340 --> 41:37.640
Can't you just speak to me nicely?

707
41:40.230 --> 41:41.630
I'm tired of coddling you.

708
41:41.820 --> 41:44.340
Why are you even here? Doesn't look like you want to be a cop.

709
41:45.200 --> 41:46.290
I do want to be one.

710
41:47.600 --> 41:50.290
Then show me what you've got, loser.

711
41:57.140 --> 41:59.890
I, Mungkorn Phianwanich,

712
41:59.920 --> 42:00.920
am no loser.

713
42:32.220 --> 42:33.080
I did it.

714
42:33.890 --> 42:34.750
I did it.

715
42:36.060 --> 42:37.220
I did it, sir!

716
42:40.060 --> 42:41.650
I did it!

717
42:47.060 --> 42:49.360
Sorry, I got a bit carried away.

718
42:50.270 --> 42:52.060
I didn't think I could actually do it.

719
42:52.660 --> 42:53.590
It's alright.

720
42:54.130 --> 42:55.110
You did great.

721
43:32.170 --> 43:33.100
Excuse me.

722
43:33.120 --> 43:34.290
Mmm, you did well.

723
43:34.740 --> 43:36.180
- Thank you. - Go take a break.

724
43:42.100 --> 43:44.320
Well, well, look at our star trainee. What's up?

725
43:46.440 --> 43:49.260
Thank you for giving me the courage to jump.

726
43:50.100 --> 43:52.050
I'm actually terrified of heights.

727
43:54.140 --> 43:55.410
I didn't really do anything.

728
43:55.700 --> 43:56.900
You jumped on your own.

729
43:57.790 --> 43:59.310
Well, you scolded me until I stepped up.

730
43:59.350 --> 44:00.490
That's why I dared to jump.

731
44:00.860 --> 44:01.980
I don't like being challenged.

732
44:02.650 --> 44:05.190
Yeah, I think we'll get along.

733
44:05.220 --> 44:07.280
Just like me. I hate being challenged, too.

734
44:07.310 --> 44:09.340
If anyone challenges me, it's on.

735
44:12.220 --> 44:15.170
You really can't judge someone based on a first impression.

736
44:16.080 --> 44:18.170
I seriously hated you at first.

737
44:18.690 --> 44:20.860
I thought you were such a poser.

738
44:23.840 --> 44:25.610
I'm still acting like one, though.

739
44:26.360 --> 44:27.300
So you like me now?

740
44:28.600 --> 44:29.830
I've started to figure you out.

741
44:30.690 --> 44:33.170
I can just let it go now.

742
44:34.650 --> 44:35.810
Are you insulting me?

743
44:38.650 --> 44:39.930
You don't have to like me,

744
44:40.520 --> 44:41.800
but just don't hate me.

745
44:59.620 --> 45:01.300
I'll go take a shower then.

746
45:03.240 --> 45:04.320
Go ahead. Get some rest.

747
45:07.160 --> 45:09.130
I told you I'd take care of this one myself.

748
45:10.000 --> 45:11.520
So why the hell are you trying to steal him from me?

749
45:13.060 --> 45:15.070
What are you talking about? When did I ever try to steal him?

750
45:15.280 --> 45:16.410
It's pretty obvious

751
45:16.800 --> 45:18.290
that you're hitting on him.

752
45:18.310 --> 45:19.860
Even after I said I wanted him.

753
45:20.400 --> 45:21.950
Bullsh*t. That's not true at all.

754
45:21.970 --> 45:23.950
I'm just talking to him like any other junior. It's nothing.

755
45:23.970 --> 45:25.250
Don't you dare lie to me.

756
45:25.880 --> 45:26.640
You

757
45:26.910 --> 45:28.650
have always loved taking things that belong to me.

758
45:28.930 --> 45:29.940
You must be thinking that

759
45:30.240 --> 45:31.740
everything comes so easily to you.

760
45:32.150 --> 45:33.950
So you think you can just take whatever you want from anyone.

761
45:34.520 --> 45:36.030
Both the job and the person I like.

762
45:36.370 --> 45:38.440
Damn, you've really lost it. That's not it, man.

763
45:38.730 --> 45:40.070
I talk to all the juniors like this.

764
45:40.090 --> 45:41.230
I was just helping the kid out.

765
45:41.610 --> 45:43.110
I know your moves all too well.

766
45:43.360 --> 45:44.520
You'll be hitting on him in no time.

767
45:49.110 --> 45:51.160
I keep telling you, I haven't done anything.

768
45:51.750 --> 45:53.490
But who knows what will happen in the future?

769
45:53.530 --> 45:54.500
Take this, you bastard!

770
45:57.260 --> 45:58.080
You piece of sh*t!

771
46:00.460 --> 46:01.470
- What's going on? - Mungkorn.

772
46:01.500 --> 46:02.750
You almost missed the main event.

773
46:02.780 --> 46:03.670
Look at that.

774
46:03.690 --> 46:05.130
The instructors are actually fighting.

775
46:08.830 --> 46:10.110
- You bastard! - Enough, goddammit!

776
46:10.340 --> 46:11.790
Why the hell are you guys fighting?

777
46:12.060 --> 46:14.040
Have some shame. You are instructors, for God's sake.

778
46:14.590 --> 46:15.430
Bastard.

779
46:15.720 --> 46:16.590
Let me tell you something.

780
46:16.620 --> 46:19.010
If you want something, earn it yourself.

781
46:19.030 --> 46:20.220
Don't come asking me to back down.

782
46:20.250 --> 46:22.370
- You loser, you're so pathetic. - Oh, listen to this prick talk.

783
46:22.390 --> 46:23.610
- Come on then! - That's enough!

784
46:24.000 --> 46:25.400
Stop fighting already.

785
46:25.730 --> 46:26.890
You guys are friends, dammit.

786
46:26.910 --> 46:28.000
I'm not his friend.

787
46:28.910 --> 46:31.290
I'm not backing down to him ever again, no matter what.

788
46:31.880 --> 46:33.580
You're just born lucky.

789
46:34.240 --> 46:37.290
And I'll do whatever it takes to beat you.

790
46:38.260 --> 46:39.330
Just you wait and see.

791
46:45.070 --> 46:46.500
I bet they're fighting over someone.

792
46:47.040 --> 46:49.310
How hot must that person be for them to be fighting like this?

793
46:49.710 --> 46:50.440
I have no idea.

794
46:50.460 --> 46:51.390
I'm really curious now.

795
46:54.280 --> 46:55.330
Who is it?

796
47:02.810 --> 47:06.380
(Graduation Day)

797
47:06.580 --> 47:08.720
I'm off. Good luck, Mungkorn!

798
47:09.120 --> 47:10.420
Okay, see you around!

799
47:23.540 --> 47:25.110
Heading home already?

800
47:26.530 --> 47:27.210
Yes, sir.

801
47:27.940 --> 47:30.030
I've been training for months. I'm starting to get homesick.

802
47:30.560 --> 47:33.620
My mom's probably prepared a huge feast for me by now.

803
47:34.680 --> 47:37.830
I hope you got something out of training with me.

804
47:38.570 --> 47:39.690
I learned a lot, sir.

805
47:39.720 --> 47:41.870
See? I've picked up so many combat skills.

806
47:44.340 --> 47:45.820
Take what’s good and put it to use.

807
47:45.850 --> 47:49.130
Leave the bad behind.

808
47:53.220 --> 47:54.860
I'll ask for your help sometime.

809
47:55.320 --> 47:57.020
Phuwin told me you're a quick learner.

810
47:59.230 --> 48:00.240
Of course, sir.

811
48:00.620 --> 48:02.450
You can call on me anytime.

812
48:06.540 --> 48:07.390
The thing is

813
48:09.190 --> 48:11.960
I saw you fight with Instructor Saming.

814
48:12.810 --> 48:14.500
They said it was over someone.

815
48:15.320 --> 48:16.280
Is that true?

816
48:19.320 --> 48:20.170
Fighting over someone?

817
48:20.760 --> 48:22.090
Nonsense. Fighting over who?

818
48:22.220 --> 48:24.610
We've never fought over anyone.

819
48:25.220 --> 48:28.100
Our types are completely different.

820
48:28.760 --> 48:30.490
It was just a stupid argument.

821
48:30.590 --> 48:32.820
Suddenly, it was like he'd turned into a different person.

822
48:32.850 --> 48:33.880
Forget about it.

823
48:39.650 --> 48:41.800
Anyway, thank you so much.

824
48:42.970 --> 48:45.740
For making my dream of becoming a police officer come true.

825
48:46.940 --> 48:48.740
I was just a small part of it.

826
48:49.150 --> 48:52.460
In the end, it was you who made it happen.

827
48:54.080 --> 48:55.940
Oh, getting all humble all of a sudden?

828
48:56.180 --> 48:58.100
You weren't like this on the first day.

829
48:58.570 --> 49:00.300
Go on, show off a little. Go ahead, brag all you want.

830
49:02.720 --> 49:05.480
People change, you know?

831
49:07.520 --> 49:10.030
I still have many sides left for you to discover.

832
49:12.410 --> 49:14.840
♪When you smile♪

833
49:14.860 --> 49:17.270
♪And you look into my eyes♪

834
49:17.290 --> 49:21.600
♪It's too much for this heart to keep inside♪

835
49:22.210 --> 49:24.610
♪Almost forgot how to breathe,♪

836
49:24.630 --> 49:27.090
♪How could you do this to me?♪

837
49:27.120 --> 49:29.840
♪Told you to stop, but you wouldn't agree♪

838
49:29.870 --> 49:31.080
Well, I'm heading off then.

839
49:32.170 --> 49:33.140
Safe travels.

840
49:33.520 --> 49:35.140
I hope we meet again.

841
49:39.570 --> 49:44.450
♪That level of cuteness is against the law♪

842
49:44.480 --> 49:49.090
♪I must be under your spell, can I blame you at all?♪

843
49:49.380 --> 49:51.920
♪You're guilty of messing with my heart,♪

844
49:51.940 --> 49:54.240
♪Stirring up my feelings right from the start,♪

845
49:54.260 --> 49:57.180
♪The fine you'll pay is your whole heart♪

846
49:57.610 --> 50:01.550
♪You take the blame, I'll take the love part♪

847
50:03.760 --> 50:06.730
(Present day)

848
50:17.910 --> 50:18.810
Master.

849
50:19.800 --> 50:21.270
I want him to love me.

850
50:25.390 --> 50:27.080
You're too late.

851
50:28.700 --> 50:30.050
Because right now,

852
50:30.640 --> 50:33.120
his soul, his body,

853
50:34.090 --> 50:36.000
and his destiny

854
50:36.550 --> 50:39.810
are already bound to someone else.

855
50:40.500 --> 50:42.340
Then what should I do, Master?

856
50:43.940 --> 50:45.780
I don't want him to be with my enemy.

857
50:46.880 --> 50:48.480
Let me ask you one thing.

858
50:49.590 --> 50:50.990
Do you actually love him,

859
50:51.010 --> 50:54.480
or do you just want to win against your rival?

860
50:55.380 --> 50:57.300
Both, Master.

861
50:58.380 --> 51:00.350
There might be a way.

862
51:04.210 --> 51:05.980
But are you willing to trade

863
51:06.010 --> 51:10.470
all the good luck you'll ever have in your life

864
51:12.050 --> 51:13.430
for him?

865
51:19.180 --> 51:21.030
("An abuse of power"?)

866
51:21.050 --> 51:23.030
(I'm impressed by the kid.)

867
51:23.060 --> 51:24.460
(I want to get to know him better.)

868
51:24.480 --> 51:26.400
We'll see where it goes.

869
51:26.510 --> 51:27.610
Whatever floats your boat.

870
51:27.890 --> 51:28.970
Not my type.

871
51:30.470 --> 51:31.480
(You must be thinking that)

872
51:31.830 --> 51:33.320
(everything comes so easily to you.)

873
51:33.340 --> 51:35.180
(So you think you can just take whatever you want from anyone.)

874
51:35.690 --> 51:37.250
(Both the job and the person I like.)

875
51:37.270 --> 51:38.580
Stop fighting, dammit.

876
51:38.980 --> 51:40.150
You guys are friends.

877
51:40.180 --> 51:41.260
I'm not his friend.

878
51:41.730 --> 51:43.430
You're just born lucky.

879
51:44.120 --> 51:47.120
And I'll do whatever it takes to beat you.

880
51:48.350 --> 51:49.400
Are you okay?

881
51:50.070 --> 51:51.180
You could stay at my place.

882
51:51.210 --> 51:52.750
No, thanks. I don't want to impose.

883
51:52.770 --> 51:54.420
You're not imposing. Let's go.

884
51:54.920 --> 51:55.930
Let go of him.

885
51:56.240 --> 51:57.370
Leave him to me.

886
51:57.390 --> 51:58.700
What right do you have to tell him what to do?

887
51:59.000 --> 52:00.350
It's after work hours.

888
52:00.380 --> 52:02.100
Are you his boss or his husband?

889
52:04.010 --> 52:04.970
Come with me.

890
52:05.000 --> 52:06.440
Jeez, enough already!

891
52:06.460 --> 52:07.540
I'll leave on my own.

892
52:34.110 --> 52:36.390
What did he do to make you change your mind suddenly?

893
52:36.420 --> 52:37.460
But it's like...

894
52:37.490 --> 52:39.350
He's under some kind of spell, right?

895
52:40.180 --> 52:43.170
The dark magic will consume Mungkorn,

896
52:43.190 --> 52:44.930
and he'll forget who you are.

897
52:44.950 --> 52:46.720
You f*cking played dirty.

898
52:46.750 --> 52:47.680
Stay away from Saming!

899
52:47.700 --> 52:49.110
If Saming gets to sleep with Mungkorn tonight,

900
52:49.130 --> 52:50.320
I don't think things will end well for Mungkorn.

901
52:50.340 --> 52:52.740
I'll try to make him remember one more time.

902
52:55.320 --> 52:58.630
♪Let's stop wasting any more time,♪

903
52:59.020 --> 53:02.050
♪Avoiding it won't make things right♪

904
53:02.260 --> 53:04.150
♪Just end this, alright?♪

905
53:04.180 --> 53:07.160
♪Say I'm no longer the one in sight♪

906
53:07.190 --> 53:09.920
♪And that I've lost this fight♪

907
53:10.210 --> 53:14.070
♪Just say it, what are you waiting for?♪

908
53:14.100 --> 53:18.280
♪Tell me it's over, and I'll walk out the door♪

909
53:20.810 --> 53:25.310
♪Don't keep me guessing anymore♪

910
53:25.340 --> 53:28.380
♪Say it and let me go♪

911
53:28.410 --> 53:32.260
♪Tell me all I need to know♪

912
53:34.400 --> 53:38.720
♪Don't keep me hanging anymore♪

913
53:38.720 --> 53:39.720
MkvDrama.net
